// Whether a moved read after event i, up to last, contains event i. That outer
// read is declared on its own and holds the inner one in its text, so the inner
// read needs no declaration of its own: xs[c[0]] is one name, not two.
fix_inner(int i, int last) {
  int j = i + 1;
  int ok = 0;
  while(j <= last) {
    ok = fix_inner_at(i, j, ok);
    j = j + 1;
  }
} return int ok;
given fix_inner_fixture (0, 1):(1)
given fix_late_fixture (0, 1):(0)

